"""Write the portable replay page and the exact experimental protocol."""
import json,html
from controlled import OUT,FIRST,COUNT

stats=json.loads((OUT/'metrics.json').read_text())
rows=''
for label,key in [('Median output objects','output_count_median'),('Fewest output objects','output_count_min'),('Initial IDs output at the end','initial_id_outputs_final'),('New track IDs created','new_ids_total')]:
    rows+=f'<tr><td>{label}</td><td>{stats["yolo"][key]}</td><td>{stats["sam"][key]}</td></tr>'
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Dance tracking · controlled comparison</title>
<style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#10131a;color:#edf2f8;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1320px;margin:auto;padding:36px 28px}h1{font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,48px);line-height:1.15;margin:12px 0}h2{font-size:23px}p{max-width:900px;color:#b9c6d8}.tag{color:#78ddc3;letter-spacing:.14em;font-size:12px;font-weight:700}video{width:100%;border:1px solid #394252;border-radius:14px;background:#000}.controls{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:15px 0 32px}button,a.button{cursor:pointer;border:1px solid #455266;border-radius:7px;padding:9px 15px;background:#202938;color:#eef4ff;text-decoration:none;font:inherit}button:hover,a.button:hover{background:#344259}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.card{padding:24px;border:1px solid #303a4b;border-radius:14px;background:#171d28}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px}td,th{padding:12px 8px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #303a4b}small{color:#a2b2c9}a{color:#8ce6d0}details{margin-top:25px}img{width:100%;border-radius:10px}@media(max-width:850px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding:22px 14px}}</style>
<main><div class="tag">DANCE FORMATIONS / CONTROLLED TRACKING TEST</div><h1>Can we keep all 20 dancers?</h1>
<p>12 seconds, 300 frames. Every dancer is marked at the start. Cropped YOLO + ByteTrack and SAM 2.1 then run without further manual correction.</p>
<video id="replay" controls loop playsinline preload="metadata" poster="comparison_075.jpg"><source src="comparison.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video>
<div class="controls"><button onclick="document.getElementById('replay').playbackRate=.5">0.5× speed</button><button onclick="document.getElementById('replay').playbackRate=1">Normal speed</button><button onclick="let v=document.getElementById('replay');v.currentTime=0;v.play()">Replay from start</button><a class="button" href="comparison.mp4" download>Download video</a></div>
<div class="cards"><section class="card"><h2>Read the comparison</h2><p>Left: overlapping image crops make each dancer larger for YOLO. ByteTrack connects detections over time. Labels beginning with N are new IDs.</p><p>Right: SAM 2 propagates the 20 prompted masks. A persistent ID can still drift to the wrong pixels.</p><p>Both maps use the bottom centre of each box and the same seven-frame smoothing. Grey points are raw positions. Hollow dots fill short gaps of at most four frames. Dots outside the mat are counted rather than clamped onto it.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Output diagnostics</h2><table><thead><tr><th>After initialization</th><th>YOLO</th><th>SAM 2</th></tr></thead><tbody>ROWS</tbody></table><p><strong>These are output counts, not accuracy scores.</strong> A mask may follow a reflection or only part of a person. Watch the overlays before judging the maps.</p></section></div>
<h2>What this test establishes</h2><p>Look for missing dancers, duplicated people, changed IDs and masks that drift. Then check whether each map dot stays near the dancer’s actual support point. Smoothing cannot repair a wrong support point.</p>
<p>The same draft full-mat calibration is used on both sides. Map coordinates are relative; the displayed mat aspect ratio is assumed. This is a controlled inference test, with no model training and no corrections after the initial frame.</p>
<details><summary>See the 20 starting marks</summary><img src="initialization.jpg" alt="The 20 manually marked dancers in the starting frame"></details>
<details><summary>Inspect later frames</summary><p><a href="comparison_075.jpg">3 seconds</a> · <a href="comparison_150.jpg">6 seconds</a> · <a href="comparison_225.jpg">9 seconds</a> · <a href="comparison_299.jpg">Final frame</a></p></details>
<p><a href="metrics.json">Full diagnostics</a> · <a href="protocol.json">Experiment protocol</a> · <a href="source.mp4">Source clip</a></p></main></html>'''.replace('ROWS',rows)
page=page.replace('<div class="cards">','''<div class="controls"><button onclick="let v=document.getElementById('replay');v.src='comparison.mp4';v.play()">Same box-bottom rule</button><button onclick="let v=document.getElementById('replay');v.src='comparison_maskanchor.mp4';v.play()">SAM mask-bottom alternative</button><small>The alternative changes only the SAM map anchor. Tracking is identical.</small></div><div class="cards">''',1)
page=page.replace('<h2>What this test establishes</h2>','''<section class="card" style="margin-top:24px"><h2>What we actually found</h2><p><strong>Neither method is reliable enough for automatic formation scoring yet.</strong> Cropped YOLO often detects fewer than 20 people and fragments their IDs. SAM keeps more masks, but some masks follow the same dancer or only a body part.</p><p>At roughly 6 seconds, inspect SAM IDs 18 and 20 in the right-hand group: they overlap the foreground dancer. In the last frame, IDs 7/9 and 10/11 also demonstrate why retaining an ID does not prove correct tracking. Upper-body masks produce false depth changes when projected onto the floor.</p><p>The mask-bottom alternative improves the typical error in the limited first-three-second contact check, but does not remove large jumps over the full clip. That check uses existing approximate labels and is not an independent accuracy benchmark.</p><p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> SAM is useful as an annotation starting point. Correct its masks and identities before using them as labels. Keep floor-contact points and visibility labels separate; neither a box centre nor a mask boundary is a dependable contact estimator during every pose.</p></section><h2>What this test establishes</h2>''')
(OUT/'START_HERE.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
protocol={'source_frames_inclusive':[FIRST,FIRST+COUNT-1],'original_seconds':[FIRST/25,(FIRST+COUNT)/25],'fps':25,'frames':COUNT,'initial_people':20,
'initialization':'20 manually placed boxes initialize both methods. SAM also uses one positive torso/head point, other dancers as negative points, and two negative points below each initial box. Prompts adjusted on first-frame smoke checks only.',
'yolo':'Pretrained yolo26m.pt; three overlapping 610x330 crops; imgsz960; confidence0.10; cross-crop IoU suppression0.65; ByteTrack high0.25 low0.10 buffer30 match0.80. Discard detections clipped at internal tile boundaries. New IDs are not remapped to lost dancers.',
'sam':'Pretrained SAM2.1-small via Ultralytics SAM2VideoPredictor; imgsz1024; FP16; 20 objects; discard detached mask components smaller than16px before deriving bounding boxes. Propagation receives no later prompts.',
'input':'Both methods consume the same decoded 1280x720 MP4 at25FPS; YOLO is seeded instead of inferred on frame0.',
'maps':'Identical bottom-centre-of-box projection and robust seven-frame local-linear smoothing; at most4-frame bounded interpolation. SAM masks have different box geometry from detector boxes. No extrapolation or clamping to mat.',
'alternative_map':'comparison_maskanchor.mp4 changes only the SAM anchor: y=99th percentile of foreground mask y; x=median foreground x in the bottom3-pixel band. Identical smoothing and tracking. This heuristic is not a verified floor-contact prediction.',
'calibration':'Existing calibration_draft.json, fixed for both methods. Full mat, assumed1.6 display aspect ratio; no metric dimensions. Copy included.',
'limitations':'Not a new held-out accuracy benchmark. First3seconds overlap previous reviewed75-frame clip. Output counts and persistent IDs do not prove correct tracks. Existing approximate visible-contact references provide a limited sanity check only. Map-step diagnostics mix real movement and noise; they are not true jitter measurements.',
'manual_corrections_after_frame0':0}
(OUT/'protocol.json').write_text(json.dumps(protocol,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
import shutil
shutil.copy2(OUT.parent/'Dance_CVAT_Pilot/calibration_draft.json',OUT/'calibration_draft.json')
print('Portable comparison page ready:',OUT/'START_HERE.html')
